---
import { ClientRouter } from 'astro:transitions';
import BaseHead, { type Props as HeadProps } from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../components/SiteFooter.astro';
import SiteNav from '../components/SiteNav.astro';

export type Props = HeadProps;

const { ...head } = Astro.props;
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en" class="antialiased">
    <head>
        <BaseHead {...head} />
        <ClientRouter />
    </head>
    <body class="min-h-dvh">
        <!--
          THESIS: A portfolio as a botanical folio — every work a numbered specimen plate grown
          from seed to husk; refuses the dark SaaS card grid and the résumé-timeline default.
          OWN-WORLD: plate-cream #F6F1E6 field, hairline sepia rules, leaf-green ink, lilac bloom
          accent (user pin retuning the folio's scarlet), engraved serif display with italic plate
          names, small-caps stage labels, arched plate frames.
          STORY: Visitor reads the name as the title plate, follows works as life stages, believes
          an engineer who grows systems in the open, reaches him by email.
          FIRST VIEWPORT: split-letter DANKE HIDAYAT title plate at full display scale over a
          botanical spore field, positioning line, featured work as an arched plate right,
          primary CTA, functional stage strip at fold.
          FORM: user-pinned whole-site rebuild — saglitz.com motion intensity (pinned scrub,
          velocity marquees, botanical particles) inside the pinned Botanical Folio world;
          functional nav vocabulary site-wide (About/Folio/Experience/Contact), folio flavor
          kept decorative only (plate numbers, captions, marquees); plates chapter 003 kept as
          designed; toolbox cut (stack lives per-plate on /folio); experience/credentials/
          contact/footer reinvented; no seed roll — user pin overrides the deal · prior seed key
          68ad9b11 stands for the world; light-first with working dark toggle (owner decision).
          Owner amendments 2026-09-24: works imagery = botanical plates kept as folio framing +
          an infinite screenshot-slot marquee (marked pending — never fabricated); navbar
          redesigned to a full-width hairline running head; theme toggle icon-only; nav brand
          reads "Danke".
          Round-2 amendments 2026-09-24: nav order About · Works ▾ · Danke (center) ·
          Florilegium · Atelier with Works dropdown (Contact left the desktop nav —
          reachable at #contact); home Works chapter = full-scroll set-piece with
          full-bleed screenshot band; About + Contact = full-viewport chapters (Contact
          gets a GSAP bloom + email baseline wipe); footer = full-screen animated
          colophon; /folio gains an editorial contents table; Florilegium (was /shelf)
          + Atelier (was /setup) redesigned at landing quality (folio hero, stats/specs
          ledgers, arched desk covers, double-rule specimen cards) — all content from
          real data, no fabrication. Compact-nav retraction: the pre-compact nav
          footprint stands.
          Round-5 (2026-09-26): Works renamed Folio everywhere (nav, footer, route
          /folio with /works redirects; hero reads "The folio."); Leafing overdrive —
          shared-element view transitions pair plates (plate-<id>) and covers
          (cover-<id>) across home/folio/florilegium soft navigations, with a hairline
          route sweep on every swap.
          FINISH: unreviewed and undocumented is unfinished; this build ends with the finish review, the verdict, and DESIGN.md
        -->
        <a class="skip-link" href="#main">Skip to content</a>
        <canvas class="spore-field" data-spores aria-hidden="true"></canvas>
        {/* Route sweep (Leafing): a hairline that draws across under the
            running head after every soft navigation, then fades. Only
            animated on astro:after-swap — first paint stays still. */}
        <div class="route-sweep" aria-hidden="true"></div>
        <div class="flex min-h-dvh flex-col site-frame">
            <SiteNav />
            <main id="main" class="grow">
                <slot />
            </main>
            <SiteFooter />
        </div>
        <script>
            import '../scripts/motion.ts';
        </script>
    </body>
</html>
